# The boards on this bench: `name  MAC  [hub  port]  [flags]  [# why]`.
#
# Copy to `devices.list` (gitignored) and put your own in. Every script that can
# write to or power-cycle a device looks the board up here first, because
# /dev/ttyACM<n> numbering shuffles between plug-ins and a guard keyed to
# anything but the MAC is one replug away from protecting the wrong device.
#
# **The same file and the same scripts as the `moisture` and `lightning`
# projects**, deliberately. Those benches share a workstation and a USB hub with
# this one, so a wren-rs script that did not know about their boards could
# happily reflash one. `tools/board.sh` and `tools/power.sh` are carried over
# unchanged for that reason -- the guard is only worth having if every project
# on the bench uses it.
#
# The MAC is on the by-id path the board enumerates as:
#
#     ls /dev/serial/by-id/
#     usb-Espressif_USB_JTAG_serial_debug_unit_AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF-if00
#                                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
#
# ## flags
#
#   forbidden   never write to it, never cut its power, wherever it is plugged.
#               For a device belonging to another project, or a live one whose
#               interruption costs more than the convenience of reaching it.
#               The text after `#` is quoted back when a script refuses.
#
# The first entry is the default when no name is given.

# name       MAC                  flags       # why
c6           AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF                # the development board

# **List the other projects' boards here too, flagged.** They are on the same
# hub; this is what stops a wren-rs flash from landing on a live sensor.
# lightning  B0:A6:04:06:E6:D4    forbidden   # a live lightning monitor, another project
# mcp        10:BD:A3:CF:3D:A0    forbidden   # the moisture control panel
# relay      80:F1:B2:51:36:E8    forbidden   # the moisture relay
# ls         AC:27:6E:5C:38:84    forbidden   # the moisture large sensor
